---
/**
 * THE TRANSLATION NOTICE. Antonio's idea, 2026-08-04.
 *
 * His brief: when someone lands on the Portuguese or Spanish site, tell them
 * once that the original is English and that this version is AI-assisted, ask
 * them to be gentle about anything that reads wrong, and invite them to
 * report it. He suggested a light joke about the robot team, which is right:
 * an apology reads as a warning about quality, a joke reads as confidence
 * plus honesty, and honesty about how this was made is the same instinct that
 * made the site say "no official answer exists" instead of inventing one.
 *
 * IT TOOK THREE DRAFTS AND THE THIRD IS THE RIGHT ONE.
 *
 * Draft 1 said "our team of robots". Antonio: "otherwise it seems like
 * everything is made by AI, and it is not." Correct, and the cost would have
 * dwarfed the joke. This site's whole trust argument is human experience,
 * almost four decades of it, written by DJs who have stood next to the
 * failure. A visitor's first sentence in their own language saying "robots"
 * hands that away, and no amount of good copy downstream buys it back.
 *
 * Draft 2 led with the DJs and demoted the machines to a joke. Better, still
 * wrong, and Antonio saw why: "you can even take out AI or robots if you
 * want. The important thing is to let them know that this is made with love.
 * It's not perfect, we'll never be, but we want it to be every time close to
 * perfection, and their help is very welcome."
 *
 * That is the whole message, and none of it depends on the method. Naming the
 * tooling up front does active harm: it makes a reader scan for mistakes
 * instead of reading, and it invites them to discount the content before the
 * first paragraph. We do not tell anyone which text editor the English was
 * written in either. Nothing here is a lie by omission: the notice says
 * plainly that the original is English and that this version is new, and if
 * anyone asks how it was made we answer straight.
 *
 * What is left is the truth that matters to the reader: this was made with
 * care, it is not perfect yet, and their correction is genuinely wanted. That
 * is also the brand's oldest instinct, the same one behind "no official
 * answer exists" and "made by DJs for DJs": say the honest thing, then ask
 * the community for help.
 *
 * FOUR RULES IT OBEYS, all of them load-bearing:
 *
 * 1. NEVER IN AN EMERGENCY. It does not render on /emergency, anywhere under
 *    /protocol, or on the outcome pages. The Emergency Engine's founding rule
 *    is that nothing competes with the decision on screen, and a DJ two
 *    minutes from a set does not need a note about translation quality. This
 *    is enforced in the component, not left to whoever adds a page.
 *
 * 2. ONCE, EVER, PER LANGUAGE. Dismissal is remembered in localStorage. A
 *    notice that returns is an interruption, not a courtesy.
 *
 * 3. IT IS A STRIP, NOT A MODAL. Nothing is blocked, nothing is centred over
 *    the page, no overlay. It sits in the flow at the top of main and can be
 *    ignored completely.
 *
 * 4. IT SHIPS HIDDEN AND IS REVEALED BY SCRIPT. Rendering it visible and
 *    hiding it on load would move the page after paint, which is the layout
 *    shift we just spent a pass removing. Hidden first, shown only if the
 *    visitor has not dismissed it, so a returning reader never sees a flash.
 *
 * The report link is a mailto, deliberately: /feedback does not exist in
 * Portuguese or Spanish yet, and sending someone who just read a sentence in
 * their own language to an English form would undo the point of the notice.
 */
import { DEFAULT_LANG } from '../i18n/registry';

interface Props {
  lang: string;
  /** English canonical path of the page, used only to stay out of the flow. */
  path: string;
}
const { lang, path } = Astro.props;

// Rule 1, in code. Extend this list rather than adding conditions at call sites.
const SILENT = ['/emergency', '/protocol', '/saved', '/files-lost', '/card-ready'];
const inEmergency = SILENT.some((p) => path === p || path.startsWith(p + '/'));
const show = lang !== DEFAULT_LANG && !inEmergency;

const COPY = {
  pt: {
    lead: 'O Save My Gig nasceu em inglês. Esta versão foi feita com carinho, mas ainda não está perfeita. Se alguma palavra soar estranha, conta pra gente.',
    joke: '',
    ask: '',
    cta: 'Falar com a gente',
    subject: 'Versão em português: uma sugestão',
    close: 'Fechar aviso',
  },
  es: {
    lead: 'Save My Gig nació en inglés. Esta versión fue hecha con cariño, pero todavía no está perfecta. Si alguna palabra suena rara, cuéntanos.',
    joke: '',
    ask: '',
    cta: 'Escríbenos',
    subject: 'Versión en español: una sugerencia',
    close: 'Cerrar aviso',
  },
};
const c = COPY[lang];
---
{show && c && (
  <div class="tx-notice" id="txNotice" data-lang={lang} hidden>
    <div class="tx-body">
      <p class="tx-lead">{c.lead} <a
        class="tx-cta"
        href={`mailto:info@savemygig.com?subject=${encodeURIComponent(c.subject)}`}
        data-event="translation_report"
        data-lang={lang}
      >{c.cta}</a></p>
    </div>
    <button type="button" class="tx-close" id="txClose" aria-label={c.close}>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>
    </button>
  </div>
)}

{show && c && (
  <script is:inline define:vars={{ lang }}>
    (function () {
      var el = document.getElementById('txNotice');
      if (!el) return;
      var KEY = 'SMG_TX_NOTICE_' + lang;
      var seen = false;
      try { seen = localStorage.getItem(KEY) === '1'; } catch (e) { /* private mode */ }
      // Shown only when unseen. A returning reader never gets a flash because
      // the element ships hidden and is only ever revealed, never hidden back.
      if (!seen) el.hidden = false;
      var close = document.getElementById('txClose');
      if (close) close.addEventListener('click', function () {
        el.hidden = true;
        try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, '1'); } catch (e) { /* nothing to do */ }
      });
    })();
  </script>
)}

<style is:global>
  /* The layout renders this above the page's own .wrap, so it carries the
     site container itself. Padding-bottom only: the page below already
     brings --page-top. */
  .tx-wrap {
    max-width: var(--site-w); margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--page-top) var(--site-pad) 0;
  }
  .tx-wrap:empty { display: none; }

  /* Quiet by construction: the amber rail marks it as information, the same
     way the site's advisory panels do, and nothing here competes with the
     page's own first heading. */
  /* NO COLOURED RAIL. The first version used the amber rail the site's
     advisory panels use, which was wrong on the site's own terms: amber means
     "this is costing you". This is a welcome, not a warning, so it takes the
     plain panel treatment and lets the link carry the only colour. */
  .tx-notice {
    display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.75rem;
    border: var(--stroke) solid var(--edge);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surf-1);
    padding: 0.7rem 0.75rem 0.7rem 0.85rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
  }
  .tx-notice[hidden] { display: none; }
  .tx-body { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; }
  /* HEIGHT IS A FEATURE HERE. The first version was three blocks and cost
     227px at 390px wide, which pushed the homepage's third door BELOW THE
     FOLD on a 360x740 Android, the exact device class the homepage CSS calls
     out as common in Brazil. A note about translation quality is not worth a
     door. One paragraph, inline link, tighter box: about 110px. */
  .tx-lead {
    margin: 0; font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--text-dim);
  }
  .tx-joke {
    margin: 0 0 0.55rem; font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--text-dim);
  }
  .tx-cta {
    font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--red); text-decoration: none;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .tx-cta:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .tx-close {
    flex: 0 0 auto; width: 44px; height: 44px; margin: -0.5rem -0.4rem 0 0;
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    background: none; border: 0; color: var(--text-faint); cursor: pointer;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  .tx-close:hover { color: var(--text); }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .tx-lead, .tx-joke { font-size: 0.82rem; }
  }
  @media print { .tx-notice { display: none !important; } }
</style>
